    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _find_enclosing_class (dart.py:662-664) checks class_definition, mixin_declaration and extension_declaration, not enum_declaration. `enum Color { red, green; final int x = 1; String describe() {...} int get code => 1; }` gives field Color.x but method describe and getter code; a top-level describe() is then indistinguishable by name. The docstring says getters and setters hash over the owner-qualified name (L35-37). r29, v10."  # 5dfc
